[
    {
        "content": "<p>For a relation <code>r : X → X → Prop</code>, define <code>predecessors r y := { x | r x y }</code>. Now suppose <code>IsStrictTotalOrder X r</code> and <code>∀ x, (predecessors r x).Finite</code>. Define <code>rank r x := (predecessors r x).ncard</code>. Then <code>rank r</code> is a bijection from <code>X</code> to either <code>Fin n</code>, if <code>X</code> is finite and <code>n</code> is its cardinality, or <code>ℕ,</code> if <code>X</code> is infinite.   Is there such a theorem in mathlib?</p>",
        "id": 628546931,
        "sender_full_name": "Ching-Tsun Chou",
        "timestamp": 1790911115
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It sounds like you're looking for <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Ordinal.typein#doc\">docs#Ordinal.typein</a> or <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Ordinal.type#doc\">docs#Ordinal.type</a> (or if you want to generalize beyond linear orders you can try <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Order.height#doc\">docs#Order.height</a>), but it's hard to say exactly how you should use it without seeing the use-case.<br>\nCould you share an example where you need this fact?</p>",
        "id": 628549003,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1790912188
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>My instinct says that the conditions given here is spelled as <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=LocallyFiniteOrderBot#doc\">docs#LocallyFiniteOrderBot</a> in mathlib</p>",
        "id": 628549251,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1790912329
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>But I couldn't find related lemma</p>",
        "id": 628549268,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1790912337
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Indeed, but assuming <code>IsWellOrder X r</code> generalizes the result beyond <code>Fin</code>/<code>ℕ</code> to any ordinal<br>\n(and <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/39427\">#39427</a> shows <code>LocallyFiniteOrderBot</code> → <code>WellFoundedLT</code>, showing it is a generalization)</p>",
        "id": 628549657,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1790912593
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks for the pointers.  At present I don't yet know if I really need this result.  I'm looking ahead while exploring formalization options.  But I do know that I won't need the general ordinal version.</p>",
        "id": 628550822,
        "sender_full_name": "Ching-Tsun Chou",
        "timestamp": 1790913373
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Here's at least how you prove this with ordinals:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FinitePredecessors</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">finite</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Finite</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsStrictOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">FinitePredecessors</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WellFounded</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">constructor</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">WellFoundedOn</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">acc_iff_wellFoundedOn</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Relation</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">transGen_eq_self</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">FinitePredecessors</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">finite</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">wellFoundedOn</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsStrictTotalOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">FinitePredecessors</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsWellOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsStrictTotalOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">FinitePredecessors</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">scoped</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ordinal</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FinitePredecessors</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">typein_eq_ncard</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ordinal</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">typein</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ncard</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ordinal</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">card_eq_nat</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ordinal</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">card_typein</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">cast_ncard</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">FinitePredecessors</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">finite</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FinitePredecessors</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">typein_lt_omega</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ordinal</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">typein</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ω</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">FinitePredecessors</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">typein_eq_ncard</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ordinal</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">typein_bijOn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsWellOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">BijOn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Ordinal</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">typein</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">univ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Iio</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Ordinal</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ordinal</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">typein_lt_type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Ordinal</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">typein_injective</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">injOn</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Ordinal</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">typein_surjOn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FinitePredecessors</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">typein_bij_of_finite</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Finite</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">BijOn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Ordinal</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">typein</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">univ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Iio</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">card</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">convert</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ordinal</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">typein_bijOn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ofFinite</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Ordinal</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">type_fintype</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">card_eq_